---
import Img from "../components/Img.astro";
import PostCard from "../components/PostCard.astro";
import SectionHead from "../components/SectionHead.astro";
import XpBar from "../components/XpBar.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site.ts";
import { FIREFLIES } from "../lib/sitecss.ts";
import { BuildMDURL, CodebergURL, RepoURL } from "../lib/state.ts";

const { progress: pr, posts } = await site();
const cur = pr.current;
const latest = posts.slice(0, 3);
---
<Layout path="/" section="home" description="Lorehallow is a small pixel-art fantasy MMO built around a shared world, with a Go server built in the open. Follow the build.">
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-scene" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="hero-layer hero-far"></div>
    <div class="hero-layer hero-mid"></div>
    <div class="hero-layer hero-near"></div>
    <span class="lantern-glow"></span>
    <span class="stars"></span>
    <span class="fireflies">{FIREFLIES.map((_, i) => <i class={`ff ff-${i}`}></i>)}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap hero-content">
    <h1 id="hero-title" class="wordmark"><Img src="web/logo_wordmark.png" alt="Lorehallow" max={576} eager class="wordmark-img" /></h1>
    <p class="pitch">A small pixel-art MMO where the world is already busy when you arrive.</p>
    <p class="hero-status">Pre-alpha. There's nothing to play yet: the server and this website are being built in the open, one checkbox at a time.</p>
    <ul class="cta" aria-label="Get started">
      <li><a class="button" href="/progress/">Follow the build</a></li>
      <li><a class="button button-quiet" href="/devlog/">Read the devlog</a></li>
      <li><a class="button button-quiet" href={RepoURL}>View the source</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-dusk" aria-labelledby="already-there">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <figure class="framed">
      <Img src="web/hero_scene.png" alt="A pixel-art village at dusk: a knight, a ranger, a wizard and a lantern-carrying traveller on a dirt path between timber cottages, a great oak and a stone well." max={720} />
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="kicker">The idea</p>
      <h2 id="already-there">A world that's already there</h2>
      <p>You log in, and other people are already around. Someone jogs past on the road. A group is fighting something at the edge of the woods. The town square is busy, and the lanterns are lit whether or not you're looking.</p>
      <p>Lorehallow is a small online fantasy world in the spirit of early World of Warcraft: a persistent place with zones, quests and grouping, drawn in warm, readable pixel art. It stays small on purpose. One handcrafted town that feels alive is worth more than ten empty continents.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="pillars">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead icon="shared_world" title="Five rules for every decision" id="pillars" kicker="Design pillars" />
    <ul class="cards cards-5">
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#shared_world" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>The world is shared</h3><p>Every feature should make other players more visible, more useful or more present.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#small_but_alive" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Small but alive</h3><p>One handcrafted zone that feels lived in beats ten empty ones. The world grows only once the core feels good.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#readable_art" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Readable pixel art</h3><p>Clear silhouettes, one locked palette of 33 colors, and the same scale everywhere.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#server_decides" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>The server decides</h3><p>The server owns the truth. Your client says what you're trying to do and draws what the server reports back.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#playable_milestones" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Playable every milestone</h3><p>Every phase of the plan ends with something you can launch, play and show someone.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-raised" aria-labelledby="what-youll-do">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead icon="explore" title="What you'll do" id="what-youll-do" kicker="Planned, not built yet" />
    <p class="lede">None of this exists yet. It's the shape of the game the plan is building toward, phase by phase.</p>
    <ul class="cards cards-4">
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#explore" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Explore <span class="badge badge-planned">Planned</span></h3><p>Mossy forests, a lantern-lit town and old stone ruins, small enough to learn by heart.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#quest" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Quest <span class="badge badge-planned">Planned</span></h3><p>Townsfolk with problems, a quest board, and a reason to wander a little farther each time.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#group_up" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Group up <span class="badge badge-planned">Planned</span></h3><p>Invite the stranger who's been fighting the same wolves as you. Some things go better in fives.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><Img src="icons/section_icons.png#fight" alt="decorative" k={3} /><h3>Fight <span class="badge badge-planned">Planned</span></h3><p>Real-time combat decided by the server, so what you see is what happened, for everyone.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-dusk" aria-labelledby="progress-now">
  <div class="wrap progress-widget">
    <div>
      <SectionHead icon="progress" title="Where the build is" id="progress-now" kicker="Live from BUILD.md" />
      <XpBar done={pr.done} total={pr.total} percent={pr.percent} label="Overall progress" big />
      <p>Every step of the plan, from an empty repository to the 1.0 launch, is a checkbox in <a href={BuildMDURL}>BUILD.md</a>. This page reads it on every push.</p>
      <p><a class="button" href="/progress/">See the quest map</a></p>
    </div>
    {cur && (
    <a class="current-phase" href={cur.url}>
      <Img src={`web/progress_landmarks.png#${cur.landmark}`} alt="decorative" k={3} />
      <span class="kicker">You are here · Phase {cur.number}</span>
      <span class="current-title">{cur.title}</span>
      <span class="current-goal">{cur.meta.Goal}</span>
      <XpBar done={cur.done} total={cur.total} percent={cur.percent} label={`Phase ${cur.number}`} />
    </a>
    )}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="latest-devlog">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead icon="devlog" title="From the devlog" id="latest-devlog" kicker="Latest posts" />
    {latest.length > 0 ? (
    <div class="post-list post-list-3">{latest.map((p) => <PostCard post={p} />)}</div>
    ) : (
    <div class="empty">
      <p>The first post is still being written. <a href="/devlog/rss.xml">Subscribe to the RSS feed</a> and it'll find you.</p>
    </div>
    )}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-raised showcase" aria-labelledby="showcase">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead icon="readable_art" title="Drawn by hand, one pixel at a time" id="showcase" kicker="The art" />
    <figure class="lineup">
      <div class="crop-lineup"><Img src="web/character_lineup.png" alt="Five adventurers standing on grass at night: a knight with a shield, a green-hooded ranger with a bow, a wizard with a glowing staff, a bard with a lute and a traveller holding a lantern." max={960} /></div>
      <figcaption>Five adventurers at the in-game scale of 32 by 48 pixels. Every sprite on this site is a text file in the repository, one character per pixel, turned into an image and checked by the build.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ul class="props" aria-label="Props from the first art batch">
      <li><Img src="props/tree_oak.png" alt="An oak tree" k={2} /></li>
      <li><Img src="props/lantern_post.png" alt="A lit lantern on a wooden post" k={2} /></li>
      <li><Img src="chars/concept_hero.png" alt="The hero: a brown-haired traveller in a green cloak" k={2} /></li>
      <li><Img src="props/mossy_rock.png" alt="A mossy rock" k={2} /></li>
      <li><Img src="props/cottage_corner.png" alt="The corner of a timber cottage" k={2} /></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="center"><a href="/world/">More of the world</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="open">
  <div class="wrap split split-text">
    <div class="prose">
      <SectionHead icon="source" title="Built in the open" id="open" kicker="Source and plan" />
      <p>All of Lorehallow is public: the Go server, the Godot client, the pixel art, the plan and every decision behind it. The server is the part this project is proudest of. It's built from the ground up to be fast, reliable and secure, and the goal is hundreds to thousands of players at once. That's a target, not a claim: no player count goes on this site until it has been measured.</p>
      <p>Every phase ends with a written walkthrough that explains the networking or backend idea behind it, so the project doubles as a course in building an online game.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="link-tiles">
      <li><a href={RepoURL}><strong>GitHub</strong><span>The source, issues and CI</span></a></li>
      <li><a href={CodebergURL}><strong>Codeberg</strong><span>A full mirror of every commit</span></a></li>
      <li><a href={BuildMDURL}><strong>BUILD.md</strong><span>The whole plan, {pr.total} checkboxes long</span></a></li>
      <li><a href={`${RepoURL}/tree/main/docs/decisions`}><strong>Decisions</strong><span>Why things are the way they are</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
